rl":"https://github.com/hidemat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hidemat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T18:35:50Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T18:54:19Z","body":"I still feel like it's needed here, since a reference to `Viewport.set_input_as_handled()` is made, someone not familiar with how godot works will think that they need to call `Viewport.set_input_as_handled()` instead of `get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()`. \r\n\r\n> If added here, it should be added onto every virtual input method, which is needlessly repetitive.\r\n\r\nWouldn't this be the case for `Viewport.set_input_as_handled()` too? If this is repeated in every input fuction:\r\n\r\n> To consume the input event and stop it propagating further to other nodes, [Viewport.set_input_as_handled()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_viewport.html#class-viewport-method-set-input-as-handled) can be called.\r\n\r\nWhy can't we also repeat the snippet?\r\n\r\nOr why don't we add a small note. Something like:\r\n> To consume the input event and stop it propagating further to other nodes, [Viewport.set_input_as_handled()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_viewport.html#class-viewport-method-set-input-as-handled) can be called. (remember to access the current [Viewport]() with [get_viewport()]())\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"h